;;
;; REPL/RedTeam/[RT-K]_PreviewParity.repl — canonical integration layout (OuronetInformational/ARCHITECTURE/REPL_AND_TESTS.md)
;;   Inter-tx:   ;;|| NEXT >  (same three lines as REPL/Stage_01/[2.2]_Core.repl)
;;   Intra-tx:   ;;==== <TX label> · mm · <slug> ====  + next-line (print "--- [<label> · mm · …] ---"); mm = 01.. within each (begin-tx …) (see OuronetInformational/ARCHITECTURE/REPL_AND_TESTS.md).
;;   format "{}": Talos / module echoes and (env-gas) — document additional prefixes in this file's (print …) lines as needed.
;;
(print "")
(print "================================================================")
(print "FILE  REPL/RedTeam/[RT-K]_PreviewParity.repl")
(print "================================================================")
(print "Legend (terminal observability): see ;; preface; echoes use <(…)> where helpful.")
(print "Source: ;;|| NEXT > between txs; ;;==== … · mm · … ==== + banner before each begin-tx.")
(print "")
;;
;; REPL/RedTeam/[RT-K]_PreviewParity.repl — FAMILY K: preview/exec divergence.
;;
;; "Does the quote tell the truth about the operation?"
;;
;; Ouronet's first rule is that an INFO preview must report the same COST as the execution it
;; previews, and `_info_measured.py` proves that for all 401 client-facing previews. Nothing checked
;; the other half: that a preview REFUSES WHEN THE OP REFUSES, and says the same thing when it does.
;;
;; A preview is what a UI calls BEFORE it submits anything. It has exactly two ways to lie:
;;   * quote a cost for an operation that cannot execute  -> the user signs, pays gas, and fails;
;;   * throw a raw internal error where the op gives a clean refusal -> the user is told nothing
;;     useful about their own pair, and a caller cannot even catch it (`try` does not catch
;;     arithmetic exceptions).
;;
;; Both were found live, in the same module family, on the same pool.
;;
;; Legend: each assertion drives the PREVIEW and the EXEC at one input and requires the SAME
;;         message from both. Either half drifting turns that one line red.
;;
;; Source: 1_SOVEREIGN/STAGE_01/2_Core/10_ATSU.pact   (URCi_* cost readers, ATSU|C>* capabilities)
;;         1_SOVEREIGN/STAGE_01/2_Core/08_ATS.pact    (URCv_RTSplitAmounts, URC_RBT)
;;         1_SOVEREIGN/STAGE_01/Z_Reads/02_INFO-ONE+.pact (INFO_ATS|* wrappers)
;;
;; REPL tests: <<RT-K-001a>> .. <<RT-K-001g>> (ATS) · <<RT-K-002a>> .. <<RT-K-002e>>  (DPTF)
;;
;; Run: cd REPL && pact "RedTeam/[RT-K]_PreviewParity.repl"
;;
(load "../deploy-stage00.repl")
(load "../deploy-stage01.repl")
(load "../Stage_01/[6.2]_DPTF.repl")
(load "../Stage_01/[6.3]_SWP.repl")

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-K-001 - does the quote refuse where the op refuses")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RT-K-001 - does the quote refuse where the op refuses · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== ==========
(print "--- [RT-K-001 - does the quote refuse where the op refuses · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [ { "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } ])
;;==== RT-K-001 · 01 · preview and exec, same input, same answer ====
(print "--- [RT-K-001 · 01 · preview and exec, same input, same answer] ---")
;;<<RT-K-001>> FAMILY: K | STATUS: FIXED
;;HYPOTHESIS: cost parity is proven for all 401 previews; REFUSAL parity is proven for none. Where a
;;            preview re-derives state instead of sharing the op's readers, the two can disagree --
;;            and an ATS pair with a zero index and no Hot-RBT (five exist at deploy) is exactly the
;;            input that separates them.
;;METHOD:     drive INFO_ATS|<op> and TS01-C2::ATS|C_<op> at the SAME arguments and require the same
;;            message from both. Non-vacuity last: the same preview on a HEALTHY pair must still
;;            return a quote, or these lines only prove that previews throw.
;;RESULT:     CONFIRMED, then FIXED. THREE of seven ATS ops diverged, in three different ways:
;;            Fuel's preview QUOTED a success the op refuses; ColdRecovery's threw a raw table
;;            error naming a composite key and the caller's full account; DirectRecovery's threw
;;            an arithmetic exception. HotRecovery's refused for a different (though true) reason
;;            than the op. Only Coil and Curl already agreed -- because their guard lives in a
;;            reader BOTH paths share, which is the whole lesson. All seven now refuse in
;;            identical words, and a healthy pair still quotes normally.
;;
;;WHAT WAS FOUND, of seven ops swept:
;;
;;   Coil, Curl        parity already -- their guard lives in URC_RBT, which BOTH paths share.
;;   Fuel              the preview returned a FULL QUOTE, ignis-need 0.53, with the post-text
;;                     "Succesfully fueled 100.0 BI-... into ATS-Pair Bisthanium-..." for an op
;;                     C_Fuel refuses outright. A confident prediction of success for something
;;                     that cannot happen.
;;   ColdRecovery      the preview threw `No value found in table ouronet-ns.ATS_ATS|Ledger for
;;                     key: <pool>|<the caller's full 162-char account>` -- a raw table error that
;;                     also prints the account back at them.
;;   DirectRecovery    the preview threw `Arithmetic exception: div by zero, decimal`.
;;   HotRecovery       both refused cleanly but for DIFFERENT reasons -- the preview named the
;;                     missing Hot-RBT, the op named the toggle. Both true; still a divergence.
;;
;;AND THE BUG HAD THREE LAYERS, which is the part worth remembering. DirectRecovery carried it in
;;the exec (fixed first), again in `URCi_DirectRecovery` (its own eager `let`), and AGAIN in
;;`INFO_ATS|DirectRecovery`, whose wrapper re-derives `release-amounts` before it ever calls the
;;cost reader. Fixing the first two left the quote still throwing.
;;
;;THE REPAIRS ARE ALL "SHARE THE GUARD", NEVER "COPY THE MESSAGE":
;;   * `UEV_FuelableIndex` -- new module-local helper, called by ATSU|C>FUEL *and* URCi_Fuel, so the
;;     message exists once;
;;   * the Cold/Direct/Hot previews call `ref-ATS::UEV_*RecoveryState` -- the very function their
;;     capabilities call;
;;   * `URCv_RTSplitAmounts` gets the zero-index guard once, covering all TEN of its call sites;
;;   * `INFO_ATS|DirectRecovery` binds its cost reader FIRST, so the op's gate runs before the
;;     wrapper's own derivations.
;;
;;==== RT-K-001 - does the quote refuse where the op refuses · 02 · let / invocation ==== =========
(print "--- [RT-K-001 - does the quote refuse where the op refuses · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (pool:string "Bisthanium-98c486052a51")
        (rt:string "BI-98c486052a51")
        (healthy:string "ComatiCommand-98c486052a51")
        (r:module{TalosStageOne_ClientTwoV2} TS01-C2)
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect
                (format "<<RT-K-001a>> the separating input, measured: {} has index {} and no Hot-RBT"
                    [pool (ouronet-ns.ATS.URC_Index pool)])
                [0.0 false]
                [ (ouronet-ns.ATS.URC_Index pool) (ouronet-ns.ATS.URC_IzPresentHotRBT pool) ])
            ;;--- Fuel: the preview used to QUOTE this successfully ---
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-001b>> Fuel  · PREVIEW" "Fueling requires an ATS-Pair Index of at least 0.1"
                (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_ATS|Fuel KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool rt 100.0))
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-001b>> Fuel  · EXEC   (same message)" "Fueling requires an ATS-Pair Index of at least 0.1"
                (r::ATS|C_Fuel KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool rt 100.0))
            ;;--- Coil: parity was already there, because both paths share URC_RBT ---
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-001c>> Coil  · PREVIEW" "Coiling requires an ATS-Pair Index greater than zero"
                (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_ATS|Coil KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool rt 100.0))
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-001c>> Coil  · EXEC   (same message)" "Coiling requires an ATS-Pair Index greater than zero"
                (r::ATS|C_Coil KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool rt 100.0))
            ;;--- ColdRecovery: the preview used to leak a composite key and the caller's account ---
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-001d>> Cold  · PREVIEW" "Cold Recovery for ATS Pair"
                (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_ATS|ColdRecovery KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool 1.0))
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-001d>> Cold  · EXEC   (same message)" "Cold Recovery for ATS Pair"
                (r::ATS|C_ColdRecovery KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool 1.0))
            ;;--- HotRecovery: both refused, but for different reasons ---
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-001e>> Hot   · PREVIEW" "Hot Recovery for ATS Pair"
                (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_ATS|HotRecovery KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool 1.0))
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-001e>> Hot   · EXEC   (same message)" "Hot Recovery for ATS Pair"
                (r::ATS|C_HotRecovery KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool 1.0))
            ;;--- DirectRecovery: three layers deep ---
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-001f>> Direct· PREVIEW" "Direct Recovery for ATS Pair"
                (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_ATS|DirectRecovery KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool 1.0))
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-001f>> Direct· EXEC   (same message)" "Direct Recovery for ATS Pair"
                (r::ATS|C_DirectRecovery KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool 1.0))
            ;;--- NON-VACUITY: without this, the ten lines above are consistent with
            ;;--- "every preview throws", which would prove nothing about parity at all.
            (expect
                (format "<<RT-K-001g>> the same preview still QUOTES a healthy pair (index {})"
                    [(ouronet-ns.ATS.URC_Index healthy)])
                true
                (> (at "ignis-need"
                      (at "ignis"
                          (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_ATS|Fuel KST.ANHD KST.ANHD healthy
                              (at 0 (ouronet-ns.ATS.UR_RewardTokenList healthy)) 100.0))) 0.0))
        ])
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(print "")
(print "===^^^===")
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-K-002 - the same question of the most-used family, and where the line is")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RT-K-002 - the same question of the most-used family, and where the line is · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [RT-K-002 - the same question of the most-used family, and where the line is · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [ { "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } ])
;;==== RT-K-002 · 01 · structural impossibility vs transient affordability ====
(print "--- [RT-K-002 · 01 · structural impossibility vs transient affordability] ---")
;;<<RT-K-002>> FAMILY: K | STATUS: FIXED
;;HYPOTHESIS: RT-K-001 swept ATS. The same question of DPTF -- the most-used family in the system.
;;METHOD:     drive preview and exec at a token that DOES NOT EXIST, and separately at an amount the
;;            holder cannot afford. Require the same message in the first case; in the second,
;;            record what each does and decide nothing.
;;RESULT:     CONFIRMED and FIXED for the structural case; the transient case is RECORDED, not
;;            changed. `INFO_DPTF|Burn` and `INFO_DPTF|Mint` returned full quotes narrating
;;            "Succesfully burned/minted 1.0 NOSUCHTOKEN-98c486052a51 ..." for a token that has
;;            never existed, while their execs refused with UEV_id's own message. Repaired by
;;            calling `UEV_id` inside `URCi_Burn` / `URCi_Mint` -- the readers BOTH paths share, so
;;            one wording serves both. The affordability divergence is pinned as-is under
;;            <<RT-K-002e>> for the owner to rule on.
;;
;;THE LINE THIS BLOCK DRAWS, because getting it wrong would mean bolting validation onto 401
;;previews on my own authority:
;;
;;  STRUCTURAL impossibility -- the token does not exist, the pool index is zero, there is no
;;      Hot-RBT. Nothing the caller does in this block makes the op available. A quote here is
;;      simply WRONG, and `INFO_DPTF|Burn` was returning the post-text
;;      "Succesfully burned 1.0 NOSUCHTOKEN-98c486052a51 on Account ..." -- narrating success for a
;;      token that has never existed. FIXED: URCi_Burn / URCi_Mint now call `UEV_id`, the same
;;      check the exec uses, so both refuse in one wording.
;;
;;  TRANSIENT affordability -- the balance is too low, the role is missing. These change between
;;      the quote and the submission, and that is the normal life of a quote. `INFO_DPTF|Transfer`
;;      quotes 99,999,999 BUSD against a balance of 8,929,990 and says
;;      "Succesfully transfered ...". That is defensible AS A COST QUOTE: `post-text` reads as the
;;      success TEMPLATE rather than a prediction, and a UI may well want the price before the user
;;      has funded anything. It is also arguably a dry-run failure. THAT IS AN OWNER DECISION, not
;;      mine, so <<RT-K-002e>> pins the CURRENT behaviour rather than changing it -- documented, and
;;      impossible to alter silently.
;;
;;ALSO OBSERVED, and left alone deliberately: driven at a non-existent id, `DPTF|C_Transfer` and its
;;preview BOTH give the raw `No value found in table ouronet-ns.DPTF_DPTF|PropertiesTable for key:`
;;-- they are in PARITY, so it is not a family-K divergence, but neither carries the `UEV_id` check
;;that `C_Burn` and `C_Mint` both have. That is the sibling-rule shape from RT-H-003 on a hotter
;;path, and it is recorded rather than patched here because it changes a refusal MESSAGE on the most
;;frequently called op in the system, which is exactly the kind of change that wants its own pass.
;;
;;==== RT-K-002 - the same question of the most-used family, and where the line is · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [RT-K-002 - the same question of the most-used family, and where the line is · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (bad:string "NOSUCHTOKEN-98c486052a51")
        (real:string "BUSD-98c486052a51")
        (big:decimal 99999999.0)
        (r:module{TalosStageOne_ClientOneV2} TS01-C1)
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect
                (format "<<RT-K-002a>> the separating input, measured: {} does not exist; {} does" [bad real])
                [false true]
                [ (ouronet-ns.DPTF.UEV_CheckID bad) (ouronet-ns.DPTF.UEV_CheckID real) ])
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-002b>> Burn · PREVIEW refuses a non-existent token" "does not exist"
                (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_DPTF|Burn KST.ANHD bad KST.ANHD 1.0))
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-002b>> Burn · EXEC   (same message)" "does not exist"
                (r::DPTF|C_Burn KST.ANHD KST.ANHD bad 1.0))
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-002c>> Mint · PREVIEW refuses a non-existent token" "does not exist"
                (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_DPTF|Mint KST.ANHD bad KST.ANHD 1.0 false))
            (expect-failure "<<RT-K-002c>> Mint · EXEC   (same message)" "does not exist"
                (r::DPTF|C_Mint KST.ANHD KST.ANHD bad 1.0 false))
            ;;NON-VACUITY: the guard must not have turned these previews into functions that always
            ;;throw. On a REAL token the quote still comes back.
            (expect
                (format "<<RT-K-002d>> ...and both previews still QUOTE the real token {}" [real])
                true
                (and (> (at "ignis-need" (at "ignis"
                          (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_DPTF|Burn KST.ANHD real KST.ANHD 1.0))) 0.0)
                     (> (at "ignis-need" (at "ignis"
                          (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_DPTF|Mint KST.ANHD real KST.ANHD 1.0 false))) 0.0)))
            ;;OWNER DECISION, PARKED: transient affordability. The preview quotes what the exec
            ;;refuses. Pinned as-is so the behaviour is documented and cannot change unnoticed.
            (expect
                (format "<<RT-K-002e>> DECIDED: the transfer PREVIEW still quotes {} against a balance of {}"
                    [big (ouronet-ns.DPTF.UR_AccountSupply real KST.ANHD)])
                true
                (> (at "ignis-need" (at "ignis"
                      (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_DPTF|Transfer KST.ANHD real KST.ANHD KST.EMMA big))) 0.0))
            (expect-failure
                "<<RT-K-002e>> ...while the EXEC refuses it outright -- the divergence, recorded not judged"
                "Cannot Debit DPTF"
                (r::DPTF|C_Transfer KST.ANHD real KST.ANHD KST.EMMA big true))
        ])
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(print "")
(print "===^^^===")
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-K-003 - the ortofungible family, and a guard that existed but could not run")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RT-K-003 - the ortofungible family, and a guard that existed but could not run · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [RT-K-003 - the ortofungible family, and a guard that existed but could not run · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [ { "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } { "key": "PK_Emma", "caps": [] } ])
;;==== RT-K-003 · 01 · DPOF preview vs exec at a token that does not exist ====
(print "--- [RT-K-003 · 01 · DPOF preview vs exec at a token that does not exist] ---")
;;<<RT-K-003>> FAMILY: K | STATUS: FIXED
;;HYPOTHESIS: third family swept. Six DPOF ops driven at a non-existent id, preview against exec.
;;METHOD:     same as RT-K-001/002 -- one input, both paths, compare the message.
;;RESULT:     CONFIRMED, then FIXED -- one divergence of six, and five clean negatives. The
;;            DeployAccount preview quoted a token that does not exist; its exec died on a raw
;;            VerumRoles read DESPITE ALREADY CALLING `UEV_id`, which sat in the `let` body under a
;;            binding that reads that very table. Repaired by hoisting `UEV_id` above the binding
;;            group (the third time this exact shape has been repaired) and by calling the same
;;            function from the INFO wrapper. A real ortofungible still quotes normally.
;;
;;WHAT THE SWEEP RETURNED, and the negative half is most of it:
;;
;;   RotateOwnership, TogglePause, AddQuantity, Burn, Mint
;;                    IN PARITY. Both paths give the SAME raw
;;                    `No value found in table ouronet-ns.DPOF_DPOF|T|Properties for key: ...`.
;;                    Not a family-K divergence -- the quote is exactly as wrong as the op, which
;;                    is all family K asks. The shared raw WORDING is a separate, H-class gap and
;;                    is recorded as known-open in DEFECT-LEDGER 7.3, together with the same gap on
;;                    DPTF|C_Transfer. <<RT-K-003d>> pins the PARITY, deliberately not the wording:
;;                    it must keep holding if and when that wording is improved on both sides.
;;
;;   DeployAccount    DIVERGED. The preview returned a full quote narrating
;;                    "Succesfully deployed a New DPOF Account for DPOF NOSUCHOFT-98c486052a51 ..."
;;                    -- the wrapper only ever FORMATS <id>, so nothing in it touched the token.
;;
;;AND THE EXEC SIDE WAS THE MORE INTERESTING HALF. `C_DeployAccount` ALREADY CALLED `UEV_id`. It sat
;;in the `let` BODY, three lines under a binding group whose second entry is
;;`(create-role-account (UR_Verum4 id))` -- a read of DPOF|T|VerumRoles. Pact evaluates every
;;binding in a group before the body, so the check written for exactly this input could never run,
;;and the op died with `No value found in table ouronet-ns.DPOF_DPOF|T|VerumRoles for key: <id>`.
;;
;;THIRD OCCURRENCE OF ONE SHAPE: C_Recover (fixed 2026-09-12), C_HotRecovery (RT-H-003), and here.
;;A validation placed in a `let` body cannot protect a read placed in that `let`'s bindings. The
;;guard being PRESENT is what makes it hard to see -- grep finds it, and the reviewer moves on.
;;
;;==== RT-K-003 - the ortofungible family, and a guard that existed but could not run · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [RT-K-003 - the ortofungible family, and a guard that existed but could not run · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (bad:string "NOSUCHOFT-98c486052a51")
        (real:string "V|OURO-98c486052a51")
        (r:module{TalosStageOne_ClientOneV2} TS01-C1)
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect-failure
                "<<RT-K-003a>> DeployAccount · PREVIEW refuses a token that does not exist"
                "does not exist"
                (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_DPOF|DeployAccount KST.ANHD bad KST.EMMA))
            (expect-failure
                "<<RT-K-003b>> DeployAccount · EXEC   (same message -- its own UEV_id, now reachable)"
                "does not exist"
                (r::DPOF|C_DeployAccount KST.ANHD bad KST.EMMA))
            ;;NON-VACUITY: the guards must not have turned these into functions that always refuse.
            (expect
                (format "<<RT-K-003c>> ...and the preview still QUOTES the real ortofungible {}" [real])
                true
                (> (at "ignis-need" (at "ignis"
                      (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_DPOF|DeployAccount KST.ANHD real KST.EMMA))) 0.0))
            ;;THE NEGATIVE RESULT, pinned. These two agree with their execs already; the assertion
            ;;is that they keep agreeing, not that the shared wording is good.
            (expect-failure
                "<<RT-K-003d>> Mint · PREVIEW and EXEC agree (parity pinned, wording not blessed)"
                "DPOF|T|Properties"
                (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_DPOF|Mint KST.ANHD bad KST.ANHD 1.0))
            (expect-failure
                "<<RT-K-003d>> Mint · EXEC   (same failure as the preview)"
                "DPOF|T|Properties"
                (r::DPOF|C_Mint KST.ANHD KST.ANHD bad 1.0 []))
        ])
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(print "")
(print "===^^^===")
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "RT-K-005 - the swap family: a quote that could not warn about a door it knew was shut")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 100000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RT-K-005 - the swap family: a quote that could not warn about a door it knew was shut · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== 
(print "--- [RT-K-005 - the swap family: a quote that could not warn about a door it knew was shut · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [ { "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] } ])
;;==== RT-K-005 · 01 · the chilled doors, on a pair without frozen LP ====
(print "--- [RT-K-005 · 01 · the chilled doors, on a pair without frozen LP] ---")
;;<<RT-K-005>> FAMILY: K | STATUS: FIXED
;;HYPOTHESIS: fifth family. SWP's previews are the most arithmetic-heavy in the system, so they
;;            re-derive more pool state than any other family's -- the condition under which
;;            RT-K-001's divergences appeared.
;;METHOD:     first the cheap separating input, a swpair id that does not exist: FIVE ops swept
;;            (ChangeOwnership, ToggleAddLiquidity, ToggleSwapCapability, UpdateFee,
;;            RemoveLiquidity) and ALL FIVE were already in parity, both paths giving the same raw
;;            SWP|Pairs read. A clean negative. Then the structural one that matters here: the
;;            CHILLED doors on a pair whose frozen-LP functionality is off.
;;RESULT:     CONFIRMED, then FIXED. The bad-id sweep found FIVE clean negatives. The structural
;;            one found the defect: both chilled previews died on `DPTF ID | does not exist` -- the
;;            BAR sentinel reaching a token-existence check -- for a pair whose real problem is that
;;            frozen LP is off, and whose exec does not say so until STEP 1, after step 0 has taken
;;            the initiation fee. Both previews now refuse with the door's own wording, before any
;;            money moves. The STANDARD door still quotes the same pair and amounts.
;;
;;WHY THIS ONE IS WORTH MORE THAN A TIDIER MESSAGE. `SWP|C_AddIcedLiquidity` is a DEFPACT.
;;`UEV_AddChilledLiquidity` refuses the door on a pair without frozen LP -- but it refuses in
;;STEP 1, and RT-A-002 already measured that STEP 0 SUCCEEDS AND COLLECTS THE INITIATION FEE.
;;So the quote is the only chance a caller has to learn the door is shut BEFORE paying to find out.
;;
;;And what the quote said instead was `DPTF ID | does not exist`. With frozen LP off, the frozen-
;;token getter returns the BAR sentinel, which reached a token-existence check -- a true statement
;;that names the SEPARATOR as if it were a token, about a token the caller never mentioned. Third
;;family in which the BAR sentinel has surfaced as a user-facing message (RT-H-003, RT-K-003).
;;
;;ONLY THE FROZEN-LP HALF IS CHECKED in the preview. `UEV_AddChilledLiquidity`'s other enforce
;;depends on the amounts, which the caller controls and can change between quote and submission --
;;transient, and family K validates what the caller CANNOT change (RT-K-002).
;;
;;==== RT-K-005 - the swap family: a quote that could not warn about a door it knew was shut · 02 · let / invocation ==== 
(print "--- [RT-K-005 - the swap family: a quote that could not warn about a door it knew was shut · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
(let
    (
        (pool:string "S|DLK-98c486052a51|OURO-98c486052a51|DWK-98c486052a51")
        (amounts:[decimal] [10.0 10.0 10.0])
        (pid:decimal (U|CT.UR_STOA-PID|Price))
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect
                (format "<<RT-K-005a>> the separating input, measured: frozen LP is OFF on {}" [pool])
                false (ouronet-ns.SWP.UR_IzFrozenLP pool))
            (expect-failure
                "<<RT-K-005b>> Iced · PREVIEW refuses in the DOOR'S OWN words, before step 0 can charge"
                "Frozen LP Functionality is not enabled on Swpair"
                (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_SWP|AddIcedLiquidity KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool amounts pid))
            (expect-failure
                "<<RT-K-005c>> Glacial · PREVIEW likewise -- the other untaxed door shares the gate"
                "Frozen LP Functionality is not enabled on Swpair"
                (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_SWP|AddGlacialLiquidity KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool amounts pid))
            ;;NON-VACUITY, and deliberately chosen to isolate the CONDITION rather than the function:
            ;;the STANDARD door on the SAME pair with the SAME amounts must still quote. If the guard
            ;;had been written too broadly this goes red.
            (expect
                "<<RT-K-005d>> ...while the STANDARD door still quotes the same pair and amounts"
                true
                (> (at "ignis-need" (at "ignis"
                      (ouronet-ns.INFO-ONE.INFO_SWP|AddStandardLiquidity KST.ANHD KST.ANHD pool amounts pid))) 0.0))
        ])
    ""
)
(env-sigs [])
(print "")
(print "===^^^===")
(commit-tx)
